  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Frost/freeze conditions expected late tonight \nand early Tuesday morning over portions of the western and \ncentral Alleghenies \n\nUpgraded freeze watch to warning for McKean, Potter, Elk, and\nCameron counties.  \n\nSecondary cold front crossing the I-80 corridor at midday with\nline of stratocu on the leading edge/colder air aloft. Expect \ncu to gradually fade this evening into tonight with the loss of\ndaytime heating. A gusty northwest wind 20-25kt aided by deeper\nBL mixing will also subside into tonight as high pressure \nslides southeastward from MI into western PA. Placement of sfc \nhigh becomes somewhat less favorable for frost/freeze Tuesday \nnight as it migrates eastward to the Mid Atlantic coast by 12Z \nWed. \n\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n \nKEY MESSAGE 2: Extended stretch of dry and seasonable Fall \nweather this week\n\nHigh confidence in a prolonged stretch of dry and seasonable \nFall wx this week with cool nights and refreshing afternoons\nwith low humidity. The next chance of rain is on Sunday.",
